CORE symex-driven-lazy-loading-expected-failure
Test
--function Test.prefixFound --max-nondet-string-length 30 --cp `../../../../scripts/format_classpath.sh . ../../../lib/java-models-library/target/core-models.jar ../../../lib/java-models-library/target/cprover-api.jar`
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
--
A float whose string has a prefix is found.
With --symex-driven-lazy-loading, the search for such a float reaches the
cap of 256 rounds of the conversion check and the result is ERROR. This is
caused by holding back index terms outside their strings, without which
the properties of StringSymbolicNeedles run out of memory or time.
